me  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL185: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL186: 【77†.github】  | 【77†.github】  |    |\nL187: 【78†book】  | 【78†book】  |    |\nL188: 【79†doc】  | 【79†doc】  |    |\nL189: 【80†halo2】  | 【80†halo2】  |    |\nL190: 【81†halo2_backend】  | 【81†halo2_backend】  |    |\nL191: 【82†halo2_frontend】  | 【82†halo2_frontend】  |    |\nL192: 【83†halo2_middleware】  | 【83†halo2_middleware】  |    |\nL193: 【84†halo2_proofs】  | 【84†halo2_proofs】  |    |\nL194: 【85†scripts】  | 【85†scripts】  |    |\nL195: 【86†.gitignore】  | 【86†.gitignore】  |    |\nL196: 【87†COPYING.md】  | 【87†COPYING.md】  |    |\nL197: 【88†Cargo.toml】  | 【88†Cargo.toml】  |    |\nL198: 【89†LICENSE-APACHE】  | 【89†LICENSE-APACHE】  |    |\nL199: 【90†LICENSE-MIT】  | 【90†LICENSE-MIT】  |    |\nL200: 【91†README.md】  | 【91†README.md】  |    |\nL201: 【92†rust-toolchain】  | 【92†rust-toolchain】  |    |\nL202: [Button: View all files]\nL203: ## Repository files navigation\nL204: \nL205:   *   * 【93†README】\nL206:   * 【93†License】\nL207:   * 【93†Apache-2.0 license】\nL208:   * 【93†MIT license】\nL209: \nL210: More items\nL211: \nL212: # Halo2-PSE fork with cq-lookup argument\nL213: ## Description\nL214: \nL215: This repository contains the 【94†halo2】 PSE fork (using KZG as polynomial commitment), with the addition of cq-lookup argument 【95†L. Eagen, D. Fiore, and A. Gabizon. \"cq: Cached Quotients for Fast Lookups\"†eprint.iacr.org】. Compared with the halo2 (plookup) lookup already available in the system, cq is suitable for the case that the lookup table size is huge and cannot be decomposed like 【96†Lasso†eprint.iacr.org】.\nL216: The API interface resembles the halo2 (plookup), e.g., supporting input expressions to aggregate input columns. For technical details, an example file is available at 【97†cq_lookup.rs】.\nL217: \nL218: To integrate the cq protocol with halo2, we adopt the commit-and-prove approach mainly for saving engineering efforts. The cq-lookup proof is done separately with a zk-version of the cq protocol, and then it is \"connected\" using column commitments in halo2-pse proof.\nL219: The formal definition (derivation of cq) and its proof is presented in 【98†zk_cq.pdf】. It is possible to encode the LHS of the Hab22 equation in the halo2 constraint system to further cut down prover cost, which we leave to future work.\nL220: \nL221: The implementation forks from the Halo2-PSE commit: 68b6006ac69a5eff21f8ae8a2fee9a55a8ee7ec4. The logs of change can be found in 【99†CHANGELOG_HALO2.txt】\nL222: ## To Run\nL223: \nL224: cargo run --example cq_lookup\nL225: \nL226: ## Minimum Supported Rust Version\nL227: \nL228: Requires Rust 1.73.0\nL229: \nL230: ## License\nL231: \nL232: Licensed under either of\nL233: \nL234:   * Apache License, Version 2.0, (【89†LICENSE-APACHE】 or 【100†http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0†www.apache.org】)\nL235:   * MIT license (【90†LICENSE-MIT】 or 【101†http://opensource.org/licenses/MIT†opensource.org】)\nL236: \nL237: at your option.\nL238: \nL239: ## Acknowledgments\nL240: \nL241: More details to come.\nL242: \nL243: ## About\nL244: \nL245: a halo2_pse fork enriched with support of cq lookup (proof of concept)\nL246: ### Resources\nL247: \nL248: 【71†Readme】\nL249: \nL250: License and 2 other licenses found\nL251: \nL252: 【72†Activity】\nL253: \nL254: ### Stars\nL255: \nL256: 2 stars\nL257: \nL258: ### Watchers\nL259: \nL260: 1 watching\nL261: \nL262: ### Forks\nL263: \nL264: 【73†0 forks】\nL265: \nL266: 【74†Report repository】\nL267: \nL268: ## Releases\nL269: \nL270: ## Packages\nL271: \nL272: ## Used by\nL273: \nL274: ## Contributors\nL275: \nL276: ## Languages\nL277: \nL278: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn7view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view3\",\"id\":118}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/commit/cb691115eec1d6347f163811366443232bc0a56d: Cache miss"
